After approval, the target design publishes audience-specific Markdown notes to SharePoint: an announcement for users, a technical summary for developers, and a README that preserves identifiers, decision metadata, and rollback context. The approved files become the knowledge boundary. Draft, NeedsInput, Duplicate, and Rejected records never become published truth. This distinction gives the agent a smaller, safer, and more understandable source than raw workflow history or unreviewed AI output.
